# 🔑 Final Takeaway

Java follows a predictable initialization sequence.

### Without Inheritance

```text
Static Initialization
        ↓
Instance Initialization
        ↓
Constructor
```

### With Inheritance

```text
Parent Static
        ↓
Child Static
        ↓
Parent Instance
        ↓
Parent Constructor
        ↓
Child Instance
        ↓
Child Constructor
```

Understanding this order helps you understand **what Java is actually doing behind the scenes when classes are loaded and objects are created**.

---

⭐ **Key Rule to Remember:**

> **Static things belong to the class and are initialized during class initialization. Instance things belong to objects and are initialized during object creation.**

This small concept connects directly to **OOP, inheritance, constructors, `static`, object lifecycle, and JVM behavior**.
